{"ref":"BDB, דָּבֵק","hw":"דָּבֵק","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">דָּבֵק</span></big>  <strong>adj. clinging, cleaving</strong> (to), <span dir=\"rtl\">דּ׳</span> abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">וְיֵשׁ אֹהֵב דָּבֵק מֵאָח</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 18:24\" href=\"/Proverbs.18.24\">Pr 18:24</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">דְּבֵקָה לְ</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 3:12\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.3.12\">2 Ch 3:12</a> (of cherub’s wing); of cleaving to <span dir=\"rtl\">הַדְּבֵקִים בְּ י׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 4:4\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.4.4\">Dt 4:4</a>.","next":"BDB, דֶּ֫בֶק","prev":"BDB, דָּבַק"}